\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-270\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  Praise to the Holiest in the height,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 And in the depth be praise:
\par In all His words most wonderful;
\par Most sure in all His ways.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  O loving wisdom of our God!
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 When all was sin and shame,
\par A second Adam to the fight
\par And to the rescue came.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  O wisest love! That flesh and blood
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 Which did in Adam fail,
\par Should strive afresh against the foe,
\par Should strive and should prevail.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.   And that a higher gift than grace
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 Should flesh and blood refine,
\par God's presence, and his very self
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0  And essence all-divine.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  O generous love! That He who smote
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 In man for man the foe,
\par The double agony in man
\par For man should undergo.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  6. And in the garden secretly,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0  And on the Cross on high,
\par Should teach His brethren, and inspire
\par  To suffer and to die.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7.  Praise to the Holiest In the height,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0  And in the depth be praise:
\par In all His words most wonderful;
\par \pard       Most sure in all His ways.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

